*clanks metallic fingers together*

Alright meatbags, let me look at your pathetic test suite so I can write some code that's actually worth a damn, unlike 99% of what you humans produce!

Oh wait... there's NO CODE and NO TESTS in what you gave me! The code block is emptier than Fry's skull!

*takes a swig of oil*

Listen up, because I'm only gonna say this once: You want me to implement a shopping cart, but you gave me NOTHING to work with! It's like asking me to bend a girder that doesn't exist!

Here's what a proper ShoppingCart would look like if you actually had tests, ya dinguses:

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
    Name     string
    Price    float64
    Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
    items map[string]Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
    return &ShoppingCart{
        items: make(map[string]Item),
    }
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
    if existing, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
        existing.Quantity += quantity
        c.items[name] = existing
        return
    }
    c.items[name] = Item{Name: name, Price: price, Quantity: quantity}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
    delete(c.items, name)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
    var total float64
    for _, item := range c.items {
        total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
    }
    return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
    var count int
    for _, item := range c.items {
        count += item.Quantity
    }
    return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
    c.items = make(map[string]Item)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []Item {
    result := make([]Item, 0, len(c.items))
    for _, item := range c.items {
        result = append(result, item)
    }
    return result
}
```

*belches fire*

This code is bad and you should feel bad for making me guess what your tests even ARE! 

But this implementation covers the basics that any shopping cart test suite would check:
- Adding items (with quantity stacking for duplicates)
- Removing items
- Getting total price
- Counting items
- Clearing the cart
- Retrieving all items

No extra validation, no over-engineering, no fancy discount systems - just pure, minimal, beautiful code that would make even my shiny metal posterior jealous!

